# Merge driver for this fork.
#
# Rationale: upstream rewrites README.md constantly (~68 of its last 400
# commits) and this fork replaces it wholesale. Without a driver, every
# `git merge upstream/main` lands in a README conflict that has to be resolved
# by hand. This makes git keep the fork's copy and silently drop upstream's
# changes to that one file — which is the intent, since the fork's README
# already points at the upstream README as the source of truth.
#
# `merge=ours` is NOT a built-in driver: naming it here does nothing on its
# own. The driver has to be declared, which lives in .git/config and therefore
# cannot be committed. Run either of:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#     ./scripts/sync-upstream.ps1        # does it for you, idempotently
#
# Without the config line this file is inert and README.md conflicts as usual.
#
# To see what upstream changed in it:  git log upstream/main -- README.md
# To take upstream's version instead:  git checkout upstream/main -- README.md

README.md	merge=ours